  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2019-08-28T22:40:04.293Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Some effects don't have a reasonable fallback shader - for example, a material which shows a wristwatch with information such as time since load, or a local-only camera display which requires a transparent unlit shader to actually be invisible to others, etc. Rather than doing hacks like making the mesh consist of degenerate tris and using a UV channel for vertex positions, it would be nice if we could just specify that this material should not be rendered when shaders are disabled.",
